      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763807769956,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "But this is not good enough we need to dive a bit more into\nhow spring actually works,but its essential to first know\nDI what is dependecy injection and what are bean plus IOC ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "But this is not good enough we need to dive a bit more into\nhow spring actually works,but its essential to first know\nDI what is dependecy injection and what are bean plus IOC ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "VwIp5SsB5kRnRY6WBkVt4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 508.42374950039215,
      "y": 3172.221168448612,
      "width": 979,
      "height": 900,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPP",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2113352973,
      "version": 984,
      "versionNonce": 1537852941,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763808810693,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Lets start with Bean -we will go into each one of them one by one\n1.Bean :So In java we have class which are basically user define object\nfor which we create refrences which are called object which we manage like\ncreation of object(new ObjectName) so let's see with an example\n\n\nclass Student{\n    private int age;\n    private int rollNumber;\n    private String name;\n    //getter \n    //setter\n\n}\n\n//we need to create and object to access that class:\nStudent obj1=new Student();//this is an object which is manged by us the programmer\n\n\nA bean is nothing but and object managed by spring boot /spring ,so we will have the same\nclass Student but we wont be creating its object it will be spring who will be \ncreating object and that object will be called as Bean \n\n\nclass Student{\n    private int age;\n    private int rollNumber;\n    private String name;\n    //getter \n    //setter\n\n}\n\n//Bean\n@Autowired\nStudent stu;//spring will inject the dependecy Student  to create object stu",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lets start with Bean -we will go into each one of them one by one\n1.Bean :So In java we have class which are basically user define object\nfor which we create refrences which are called object which we manage like\ncreation of object(new ObjectName) so let's see with an example\n\n\nclass Student{\n    private int age;\n    private int rollNumber;\n    private String name;\n    //getter \n    //setter\n\n}\n\n//we need to create and object to access that class:\nStudent obj1=new Student();//this is an object which is manged by us the programmer\n\n\nA bean is nothing but and object managed by spring boot /spring ,so we will have the same\nclass Student but we wont be creating its object it will be spring who will be \ncreating object and that object will be called as Bean \n\n\nclass Student{\n    private int age;\n    private int rollNumber;\n    private String name;\n    //getter \n    //setter\n\n}\n\n//Bean\n@Autowired\nStudent stu;//spring will inject the dependecy Student  to create object stu",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "342A4-odW-XGmF0pBoly9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 505.83628945471366,
      "y": 4153.303343665597,
      "width": 829.2445287201195,
      "height": 975,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPQ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1595472003,
      "version": 249,
      "versionNonce": 332544365,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763809028138,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. What Is a Bean in Spring?\n\nA Bean is simply an object created, managed, and destroyed by the Spring\nIoC Container.\n\nBean = Object created by Spring instead of new keyword\n\nExample (Without Spring):\n\nLaptop laptop = new Laptop();   // You create object\n\n\n\nExample (With Spring):\n\nSpring creates the object, not you.\n\n@Component\nclass Laptop {}\n\nThen you get it from Spring:\n\n@Autowired\nLaptop laptop;   // Spring injects object\n\n✔ A bean is just a normal class marked for Spring management using:\n\n1.@Component\n\n2.@Service\n\n3.@Repository                             \n\n4.@Controller                             this object notation  \n                                          automatically create object\n\n5.@Configuration\n\n6.@Bean",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. What Is a Bean in Spring?\n\nA Bean is simply an object created, managed, and destroyed by the Spring IoC Container.\n\nBean = Object created by Spring instead of new keyword\n\nExample (Without Spring):\n\nLaptop laptop = new Laptop();   // You create object\n\n\n\nExample (With Spring):\n\nSpring creates the object, not you.\n\n@Component\nclass Laptop {}\n\nThen you get it from Spring:\n\n@Autowired\nLaptop laptop;   // Spring injects object\n\n✔ A bean is just a normal class marked for Spring management using:\n\n1.@Component\n\n2.@Service\n\n3.@Repository                             \n\n4.@Controller                             this object notation  \n                                          automatically create object\n\n5.@Configuration\n\n6.@Bean",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
