    {
      "id": "eSwjW_OShAmcxSn-pg9YF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 459.7247317542633,
      "y": 5366.148106232166,
      "width": 1045,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1985218883,
      "version": 272,
      "versionNonce": 747226733,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763809133866,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now here intially we where manage-ing the object but as soon as spring start's managing the \nobject we are inverting the control from us to spring this is know as IOC(Inversion of control)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now here intially we where manage-ing the object but as soon as spring start's managing the \nobject we are inverting the control from us to spring this is know as IOC(Inversion of control)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rcrDCax6n1pS1W911GyIQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 461.8670725114424,
      "y": 5474.396269725363,
      "width": 671,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPm",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 422765475,
      "version": 42,
      "versionNonce": 1628889453,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763809153870,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. What Is IoC (Inversion of Control)?\n\nIoC means:\n\nYou give control to Spring. Spring creates objects, gives you\ndependencies, and manages their lifecycle.\n\nWithout IoC (normal Java):\n\nYou control everything.\n\nStudent s = new Student();  // You create\nLaptop l = new Laptop();    // You create\ns.setLaptop(l);             // You wire\n\nWith IoC:\n\nYou hand over control.\n\n@Autowired\nLaptop laptop;  // Spring injects\n\nIoC is the big idea.DI is the way it is implemented.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. What Is IoC (Inversion of Control)?\n\nIoC means:\n\nYou give control to Spring. Spring creates objects, gives you dependencies, and manages their lifecycle.\n\nWithout IoC (normal Java):\n\nYou control everything.\n\nStudent s = new Student();  // You create\nLaptop l = new Laptop();    // You create\ns.setLaptop(l);             // You wire\n\nWith IoC:\n\nYou hand over control.\n\n@Autowired\nLaptop laptop;  // Spring injects\n\nIoC is the big idea.DI is the way it is implemented.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
