      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. What Is Dependency Injection (DI)?\n\nDI means:\n\nSpring injects (gives) required objects instead of you creating them\nmanually.\n\nExample:\n\nclass Student {\n    private Laptop laptop;\n\n    public Student(Laptop laptop) {  // Dependency injected\n        this.laptop = laptop;\n    }\n}\n\nDI ≠ creating objectsDI = giving ready-made objects",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. What Is Dependency Injection (DI)?\n\nDI means:\n\nSpring injects (gives) required objects instead of you creating them manually.\n\nExample:\n\nclass Student {\n    private Laptop laptop;\n\n    public Student(Laptop laptop) {  // Dependency injected\n        this.laptop = laptop;\n    }\n}\n\nDI ≠ creating objectsDI = giving ready-made objects",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
